        "heading": "Birch working note 2",
        "content": "Birch Kite completed 110 deliveries in April. The count uses the same\ncompleted-delivery definition as the March tally.\n\nFor routine handoffs, open the checklist, mark the items already reviewed, and\nleave the remainder for the next shift. The checklist is a record of work in\nprogress, not an authorization to change the underlying arrangement. Staff can\nadd a short note when a handoff crosses a weekend or a public holiday.",
        "kind": "source_chunk",
        "last_scan_at": "2026-10-30T14:57:40.102985+00:00",
        "freshness": "recent",
        "uncertainty": "Source text has not been reviewed.",
        "citation_id": "source:3db91a5f-18b3-5127-b80f-a8488bebd592:476d0912-09fd-5906-a3ab-efbe3215df60",
        "presented_content": "Birch Kite completed 110 deliveries in April. The count uses the same\ncompleted-delivery definition as the March tally.\n\nFor routine handoffs, open the checklist, mark the items already reviewed, and\nleave the remainder for the next shift. The checklist is a record of work in\nprogress, not an authorization to change the underlying arrangement. Staff can\nadd a short note when a handoff crosses a weekend or a public holiday."
      },
      {
        "collection_id": "a0aed607-10ec-406b-82c3-b4bfcb97da1a",
        "document_id": "ee0dc143-b451-5235-a836-6035156ec2da",
